<title>GREECE: Alpha, Delos lead Greek growth funds in H1.</title>
<headline>Alpha, Delos lead Greek growth funds in H1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpha Growth and Delos Blue Chips mutual funds were leading Greece's 27 growth funds in the first half with returns of 62.87 and 62.29 percent, respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Eight funds managed to outperform the bourse's benchmark index in the first half of 1997, locking in profits in June.</p>
<p>The Athens stock exchange's general share index started the year at 954.54 and gained 563.97 points or 59.08 percent to 1,518.51 points in the six months to June 30.</p>
<p>Growth fund assets under management reached 157.2 billion drachmas in end-June, up 110.57 percent since the beginning of the year and down 2.76 percent on May.</p>
<p>They made up 3.07 percent of the mutual fund industry's total assets which rose to 5.41 trillion drachmas in the first half of 1997, an increase of 41.84 percent.</p>
